Package: DiffiScape
Title: Differentiable Landscape Connectivity Optimization via CircuitScape.jl
    and Enzyme.jl
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Sean", "Sorek", , "sssorek1@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Gradient-based and surrogate-based optimization of landscape
    connectivity surfaces. Combines circuit-theory connectivity computation
    (Omniscape.jl / Circuitscape.jl) with automatic differentiation
    (Enzyme.jl) to fit Poisson Point Process models of animal movement.
    Users supply environmental rasters and GPS locations; DiffiScape
    estimates resistance parameters that best explain observed spatial
    intensity. Supports negative binomial and GAM-based intensity models
    via 'mgcv'.
